cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this repository with the metadata below."
title: "Measured steps toward a logic-based language model with Tsetlin Machines"
abstract: >-
  This repository holds the code, the registrations and the results pages of
  three studies (19 Sep to 3 Oct 2026) that take measured steps toward a
  language model built from Tsetlin Machine clauses; run folders and datasets
  are not distributed. The first study built a token-level Tsetlin Machine
  language model on a sparse event-driven engine and compared it with a
  Kneser-Ney 5-gram model on the same tokens: its reproducibility hypotheses
  were met at the scale tested, and its main accuracy goal was missed on the
  one seed that was run, which triggered the registered kill criterion. The
  second study tested the hierarchical Tsetlin Machine procedure of an
  unpublished project proposal on artificial data, two sentence
  families, news topics and Wikipedia paragraph pairs and ended mostly
  negative: its single final test is below word overlap on both Wikipedia
  tasks. The third study is preparation for a word-level clause language
  model: count baselines and one evaluator ran without a Tsetlin Machine, and
  the reproduction of an existing Tsetlin Machine router did not meet its
  first gate in its one completed run.
